WHAT A PACKAGED KEEPER CONTAINS BESIDES KEEPER

The dmg and the exe carry other people's work inside them, so this file says
whose and under what. Running keeper from a git clone carries the same
libraries, installed by npm rather than bundled.

  Node.js                     MIT
  https://nodejs.org
  Bundled unmodified, from the official builds at nodejs.org, and the
  build script verifies the published sha256 before using one.

  sharp                       Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/lovell/sharp

  libvips                     LGPL-3.0-or-later
  https://github.com/libvips/libvips
  Bundled unmodified as a shared library inside @img/sharp-libvips-*. It
  can be replaced with another build of the same library: the file sits in
  Contents/Resources/app/node_modules on macOS and in the app folder on
  windows, uncompressed, and nothing here prevents swapping it. Source for
  the exact version is at the address above.

  Geist and Geist Mono        SIL Open Font License 1.1
  https://github.com/vercel/geist-font
  Full text in web/font/OFL.txt.

  Phosphor Icons              MIT
  https://github.com/phosphor-icons/core
  Full text in web/phosphor-LICENSE.txt.

  ffmpeg                      LGPL-2.1-or-later, when it is bundled
  https://ffmpeg.org
  Only present in a build made with --with-film. It is invoked as a
  separate program and keeper links to none of it.
